<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Władysław IV Vasa</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Władysław IV</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Władysław IV Vasa was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and Grand Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> from 1632 to 1648. In his youth he was elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> after Polish forces occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> in 1610, though he never ruled there. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> describe this episode as a moment of overreach that showed the Commonwealth's offensive reach at its peak.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/w-adys-aw-iv-vasa.jpg" alt="Władysław IV Vasa" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peter Paul Rubens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rubens_Wladyslaw_Vasa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
